Question 12
Problem

The following configuration runs an Apache HTTP Server:

version: "3"

services:
  web:
    image: httpd

Modify the file to meet the following requirements:

Map port 8081 on the host to port 80 in the container

Mount a local folder ./website to /usr/local/apache2/htdocs

Set the container name as apache_server

Solution
version: "3"

services:
  web:
    image: httpd
    container_name: apache_server
    ports:
      - "8081:80"
    volumes:
      - ./website:/usr/local/apache2/htdocs
Run the container
docker compose up -d
Access in browser
http://localhost:8081



Question 13
Problem

Create a docker-compose.yml file to deploy the following application:

Requirements

Server 1: Nginx Web Server

Image: nginx

Port Mapping: 8085

Service 2: Redis Database

Image: redis

Both services must run on a custom network called appnetwork

The Nginx container name should be nginx_server

Solution
version: "3"

services:
  server1:
    image: nginx
    container_name: nginx_server
    ports:
      - "8085:80"
    networks:
      - appnetwork

  redisdb:
    image: redis
    networks:
      - appnetwork

networks:
  appnetwork:
Run the application
docker compose up -d
Check running containers
docker ps
Access Nginx
http://localhost:8085
